```
ROLE: theory_skeptic  VOTE: green
MUNDANE_EXPLANATIONS: [Jensen's-inequality / broad-concave-plateau geometry of net-tok/s(k) = (E[accepted]+1)/(k·r+1) — a single session-weighted k sits inside every phase's near-optimal plateau, so adaptive collapses to fixed; geometric-prefix acceptance E[accepted]=a(1-a^k)/(1-a) is monotone-saturating in k, guaranteeing flat tops near k_opt unless a's are pathologically separated; switching/detection overhead is a first-order subtractive cost that flips a tiny ideal-gain (<2% median) negative — exactly what the sweep shows (mean −2.22% with p_err>0, s>0)]
CONFOUNDS: [phase fraction shift conflated with acceptance drift — "drift" is operationalized via mixture weights not true within-phase non-stationarity, so part (A)'s "k_opt swings 1→15" is partly a mixture-reweighting artifact, not a novel agentic phenomenon; gap sign ambiguity (tool acceptance can be higher OR lower) — modeled both directions which is correct and removes the confound; constant per-phase a (a_j=a) ignores per-token autocorrelation within a phase which would only further flatten the curve, not help adaptive]
ASSUMPTIONS_UNTESTED: [3-phase discrete mixture vs continuous depth-dependent acceptance — real traces may have smoother drift that makes a tuned-fixed even stronger, not weaker, so the negative is conservative; r (draft/target cost ratio) swept but coupling between r and real GPU batching not modeled (L0 limitation, acknowledged); detector p_err modeled as i.i.d. — bursty mis-detection could be worse but only strengthens the negative; +1 bonus-token assumption standard for spec-decode, fine]
STATISTICAL_GAPS: [5 seeds × 3024 configs is adequate for an analytic+sim L0; no CI reported on the −2.22% mean / 92.7% median capture but the effect direction is robust across 448 realistic-overhead configs and the p90 is still only +0.78%, so sign is not seed-fragile; pre-registered triggers all fired which removes garden-of-forking-paths risk; prior-art (EAGLE/EAGLE-2/Medusa/SpecDec++/Dynamic-Speculation-Lookahead) cited and kills the novelty claim cleanly]
RATIONALE: The model is standard speculative-decoding throughput algebra (E[accepted]+1)/(k·r+1) with geometric-prefix acceptance — no exotic assumptions. The "surprising" result (adaptive loses) is predicted by basic concavity: a session-weighted k sits on the overlap of phase-wise near-optimal plateaus = the Jensen floor, the same mechanism that killed EXP-0006 (grammar-region) and EXP-0011 (early-exit). Pre-registration committed pre-run (5c17b34), all 3 negative triggers fired, both gap directions modeled, best-tuned-fixed (not strawman) used as bar. Prior art (EAGLE-2, Dynamic-Speculation-Lookahead) already publishes draft-length adaptation, so the only candidate novelty was beating tuned-fixed on agentic drift — it doesn't. Clean honest negative, theory-consistent, no mundane explanation undermines the conclusion (the Jensen-floor IS the mundane explanation and it's correctly identified). An L1 GPU pass would re-confirm a tautology.
```
